{"id":"elimelech","name":"Elimelech","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:elimelech"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Elimelech","text":"God his king, a man of the tribe of Judah, of the family of the Hezronites, and kinsman of Boaz, who dwelt in Bethlehem in the days of the judges. In consequence of a great dearth he, with his wife Naomi and his two sons, went to dwell in the land of Moab. There he and his sons died (Ruth 1:2, 3; 2:1, 3; 4:3, 9). Naomi afterwards returned to Palestine with her daughter Ruth."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5281","lemma":"נׇעֳמִי","xlit":"Noʻŏmîy","gloss":"Noomi, an Israelitess","kjv":"Naomi","count":6,"share":1},{"strong":"H458","lemma":"אֱלִימֶלֶךְ","xlit":"ʼĔlîymelek","gloss":"Elimelek, an Israelite","kjv":"Elimelech","count":5,"share":0.83},{"strong":"H3630","lemma":"כִּלְיוֹן","xlit":"Kilyôwn","gloss":"Kiljon, an Israelite","kjv":"Chilion","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H4248","lemma":"מַחְלוֹן","xlit":"Machlôwn","gloss":"Machlon, an Israelite","kjv":"Mahlon","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H1162","lemma":"בֹּעַז","xlit":"Bôʻaz","gloss":"Boaz, the ancestor of David","kjv":"Boaz","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H7704","lemma":"שָׂדֶה","xlit":"sâdeh","gloss":"a field","kjv":"country, field, ground, land","count":3,"share":0.5}],"verses":["Ruth.1.2","Ruth.1.3","Ruth.2.1","Ruth.2.2","Ruth.4.3","Ruth.4.9"],"related":[{"id":"inheritance","type":"lexical","strong":"H5281","why":"both lead with נׇעֳמִי (H5281)"}],"works":[{"work":"antiquities","title":"Antiquities of the Jews","count":4,"chapters":[{"chapter":"AntV.9","count":4,"book":"Ant. 5","title":"How Under Eli's Government Of The Israelites Booz Married Ruth, From Whom Came Obed The Grandfather Of David."}]}]}
